findings.body:
In `_propagate_skip_to_node`, the PR moves `mark_edge_skipped(edge.id)` to after `propagate_skip_from_edge(edge.id)`. `propagate_skip_from_edge` decides based on the states of the downstream node's incoming edges, and this edge is still UNKNOWN while the recursion runs, so `has_unknown` is true and the function returns immediately.

I reproduced this with the real `GraphStateManager` and this `SkipPropagator`, using a chain `X -> B -> C` with a taken edge `T -> C`. X is skipped, which marks `X->B` skipped and calls `propagate_skip_from_edge`. With the PR ordering, `B` is skipped, `B->C` is skipped, but `C` stays UNKNOWN, is never enqueued, and the ready queue and executing set are both empty. Downstream nodes that depend on a skipped chain are therefore lost, and the dispatcher can finish with them never run. With the original ordering (mark skipped, then recurse), `C` is enqueued and started.

The `skip_branch_paths` method still uses the original order (mark, then propagate), so the two call sites are now inconsistent.

::diff{file="api/core/workflow/graph_engine/graph_traversal/skip_propagator.py" lines="81-87"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The new unit tests don't catch this because they mock `analyze_edge_states` to always return `all_skipped`, which makes the recursion independent of edge state. See the test-coverage finding below.

Revert the two lines to their original order:

::suggestion{file="api/core/workflow/graph_engine/graph_traversal/skip_propagator.py" lines="83-86"}
        for edge in outgoing_edges:
            # Mark edge skipped before recursing so downstream sees the real state
            self._state_manager.mark_edge_skipped(edge.id)
            # Recursively propagate skip
            self.propagate_skip_from_edge(edge.id)

`print(f"Starting execution for node: {downstream_node_id}")` writes to stdout on every skip-triggered enqueue. It bypasses the project's logging configuration and would appear in production worker output. The adjacent `start_execution` call already records the same fact, so the print adds nothing.

::diff{file="api/core/workflow/graph_engine/graph_traversal/skip_propagator.py" lines="60-66"}

Remove the print. If visibility is needed, use the module's logger pattern used elsewhere in `core/workflow` at debug level.
